  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 402 AM EST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nThe long term begins with a longwave trough transitioning along the \neastern seaboard, with ridging building into the northern plains. \nFor the weekend, expect the continuation of dry and cold conditions, \nwith a freeze watch likely for the majority of our CWA on Saturday \nnight. Temperatures will remain below or near seasonal norms through \nTuesday before afternoon highs increase into the low to upper 60s \nareawide by Wednesday afternoon. On Sunday, surface winds will shift \ntoward the northeast along the periphery of a high pressure system \nmoving into the Midwest, remaining so through the second half of \nnext week. Otherwise, guidance continues to showcase a shortwave \ndiving southeastward out of the southern plains, aiding the \ndevelopment of a surface low that will trek along the Gulf Coast on \nTuesday. While this system moves along the Gulf, dry northeast winds \nand broader high pressure influences will limit moisture as most of \nthe heavier showers or storms stay to the south of our area. That \nbeing said, a few stray showers can't be ruled out in our \nsouthernmost counties on Monday night into Tuesday morning. \nOtherwise, expect dry conditions with a warming trend into the \nsecond half of next week.",
